  "slug": "salesforce-event-alert-observability-and-failure-injection-tests",
  "concept": "Salesforce event-alert observability and failure-injection tests",
  "generated": "2026-11-12",
  "summary": "Source-anchored research for Salesforce event-alert observability and failure-injection tests. Run status: COMPLETED.",
  "facets": [
    {
      "title": "How it works",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Recommended timeout tests must distinguish exhausted demand from a healthy idle stream: when pending demand reaches zero the client must send another FetchRequest within 60 seconds; with pending demand and no events, the server sends an empty keepalive FetchResponse within 270 seconds. These are separate test conditions. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-12)",
          "source": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/references/methods/subscribe-rpc.html",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:5ede3f50c9adcd296bbe76022186d8dbdf9947a898cc2df1e70ed1a084f2d3eb",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:e29b9f7867e4acc089fdba0923eb6b552053b44a971649f69236772b63084c55"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Recommended observability check: alert when scheduled synthetic-test telemetry disappears, as well as when a synthetic test fails. Salesforce Commerce engineering explicitly checks that test-tenant metrics exist during every continuous-test interval; applying that pattern to case alerts is a design recommendation, not a documented Pub/Sub feature. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://engineering.salesforce.com/managing-availability-in-service-based-deployments-with-continuous-testing-61be968da4a/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:a3ada11b2f45021f2004cc758112622bf968d48ff95ec99ff0c71ac9737d7628",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:07f7a692dfa33037efa8106acaea0b1a5dd344eedcee6ea5c16dbe5685706574"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Problems, failure modes and limitations",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "For Pub/Sub failure diagnostics, retain the gRPC status, the custom error code from trailers, and the RPC execution identifier. Salesforce documents the RPC identifier as useful for support investigations. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/guide/handling-errors.html",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:8b65f65f58eda24ae4a4b3ad88bace154edd22a8b988f572c2ddd4e583c7e340",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:1e85558ceb32dbe743ca617fee35c81e9a4f235117aabba95cbf3116bc8d8a32"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Recommended failure-injection check: terminate a long-lived RPC and verify that the client starts a replacement call, limits retry attempts, and increases retry delays exponentially. Salesforce recommends bounded exponential backoff; a replacement RPC is required after the streaming connection fails. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/guide/retry-rpc-calls.html",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:24c03fa3eb29996a9ec77f221a70a46a084f372207a777f6c32d32ee3e95b0ab",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:5592227f927c85054cc38c84df45bb37844a5ef545cbddf91fc7acbf8b2e5be8"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/guide/handling-errors.html"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Apex event tests use a separate test event bus and do not execute external Pub/Sub subscribers. Consequently, passing Apex tests alone cannot validate the external case-alert delivery path. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/platform-events/guide/platform-events-test-events.html",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:b54d263f57c4a1016d2bd89900ce9533814278f21f47623d0be3bf6b03b61d71",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:814a5c62a7c33594a706767eb14686e08e76270db767f2f8545e6d6d5bc7bd84"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The independent Wolverine Salesforce transport documents per-listener heartbeat counters for uptime, responses, events, errors, reconnects, and the last success or error. These provide a concrete implementation example for an alert collector dashboard. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-12)",
          "source": "https://github.com/meyc-v1/wolverinefxcontrib-salesforcepubsub",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:74c3931ca2dd702e485144f8fdfc70502e32600541ea86029a3fff3deecfa18a",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:b73f0eab5a228628d7e4db1161a0b17ff751f2719ef95adbec17554f93793dae"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The Wolverine repository also documents crash/force-kill/restart and poison-message experiments. These are relevant failure-injection categories for an alert consumer; the repository’s observed outcomes apply to its transport and configuration, not to every Salesforce application. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-12)",
          "source": "https://github.com/meyc-v1/wolverinefxcontrib-salesforcepubsub",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:ca3840e3b35735c4cb29c09f28d2e5675e4e62aaf33df36e2b012e8b73fe191e",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:b9b6e389d29fa7d68e376c597026da146b6e26f080987a99efc3e69aa4c6e3cb"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The Node Pub/Sub client exposes subscription callback signals for parsing/stream errors, stream end, keepalive, and stream status. Recommended instrumentation should distinguish those signals so a parsing failure is visible separately from a transport lifecycle change. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-12)",
          "source": "https://github.com/pozil/pub-sub-api-node-client",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:b435f3cc589ea731ce24bf51502eac015e7fed681e5e756f3095cf3b12eaf42c",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:6c46c59aede54b470acd4ba43a0e7e9ed1d5828bcb2f15d6b32c186c45168dd5"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Poison-message test recommendation: inject an event parsing failure and verify that monitoring distinguishes it from a transport failure. The Node client documents both as possible error-callback causes. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-12)",
          "source": "https://github.com/pozil/pub-sub-api-node-client",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:77d7ff7308cd4de064fc1d3cbca700840ecb10d7591bfb921652c65e8f75c748",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:cacf778c48973913a05db5f00165a26a9b79675ef2506439268be709e9c1f297"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Comparisons and alternatives",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Independent implementations provide practical local transport-test examples: Ballerina exercises unary and streaming gRPC using a self-signed TLS fixture, while OSO runs a local fake Salesforce without requiring an org. These are examples of fixture-based tests, rather than proof that a local fixture reproduces every production behavior. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-12)",
          "source": "https://github.com/ballerina-platform/module-ballerinax-salesforce.pubsub",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:11a0fcb44b1800814fbf74e4cee3a2f925888a21912cc39b9541958fabc96eff",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:62a8ede97fa7a45395339de809c909af5debe65945f5ba3f23a9ce5ae4408910",
            "ev:ee6305a6a1f52690895e5e61dc43e631cdd2d44bbc547c378da76ce573fc363a"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://github.com/osodevops/kafka-connect-salesforce-oss/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "OSO documents a local fake Salesforce harness with an in-process Pub/Sub gRPC implementation supporting replay semantics. It is a concrete external-client test-harness lead, rather than evidence that this case-alert application has passed integration tests. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-12)",
          "source": "https://github.com/osodevops/kafka-connect-salesforce-oss",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:7d489525e24ed47af930ca2565e063a885993e26d663bf9ee08a9c3d18e8c4bc",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:dcc3b77c996f24e0f988b107f27fc2d15726e9d7d68f724188b9486b3fdbb265"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Facts and statements",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Ballerina maintains a separate live shared-org suite that is disabled by default. A successful local fixture run therefore does not by itself establish that the live sandbox suite ran. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-12)",
          "source": "https://github.com/ballerina-platform/module-ballerinax-salesforce.pubsub",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:5949ff9894548e53352e65250c8787c1716a27fe6c1d8c5a9e8c9869d39ffe2a",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:266a03c7673d03e40eebc62f6ae27a8c29b47cf11f979b8af9c4e0afda3a9faa"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Idle-stream test: while delivery demand remains outstanding and no events are available, expect an empty response as a keepalive within 270 seconds. Treat idle health separately from event-arrival activity. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/references/methods/subscribe-rpc.html",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:abd824eafa00a550b687b10e419ac0a149c40ea2f8b5f57e9e9fbc69b359fd17",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:55edc6515bdead0028e8abb1856a93ae75851a7e824a39682769afd374f37012"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Request-starvation test: after the requested batch is exhausted, verify that the client renews demand within 60 seconds. Salesforce specifies this deadline for keeping the subscription alive. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/references/methods/subscribe-rpc.html",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:35876c9c5a48093b0a52318174f602259164b1fc60ce3cc77b384a1c77c90f9f",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:659ea88f7475b99d8648977308a0a10404a6671ebd76ceb200ab644d01ca4c9f"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "OSO requires behavioral changes to have coverage against its fake harness and documents a build check with additional Docker end-to-end tests in CI. This is a useful model for layered client validation. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-12)",
          "source": "https://github.com/osodevops/kafka-connect-salesforce-oss/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md",
          "note": null,
